# Directory Structure of the brane control node

The Control Node requires a specific directory hierarchy to manage infrastructure, certificates, and runtime state. Create this structure in your home directory:

````Plaintext
~/brane-central/
├── config/
│   ├── certs/            # Contains worker domain certificates (ca.pem)
│   ├── infra.yml         # Infrastructure file (defines worker nodes)
│   ├── proxy.yml         # Proxy configuration
│   └── node.yml          # Central node configuration
├── target/
│   └── release/          # Contains central-instance-x86_64.tar.gz
└── policies.db           # Local policy database


# 2. Step-by-Step Setup
## Step A: Initialize Infrastructure

### A.1 Create the directory tree:

```Bash
mkdir -p ~/brane-central/config/certs ~/brane-central/target/release
cd ~/brane-central

## Step B: Prepare Files


Download branectl 
```bash
curl https://github.com/BraneFramework/brane/releases/download/nightly/branectl-linux-x86_64
```
NOTE: check the path shoudl "nightly"


#### B.2 Download Images: Use branectl to download the core services and auxiliary images (e.g., ScyllaDB):

```Bash
branectl download services central -f
branectl download services auxillary -f
```

### B.3 Generate Infrastructure File: Register your worker nodes (replace <ID>:<ADDR> with your worker details):

```Bash
branectl generate infra -f -p ./config/infra.yml <ID1>:<ADDR1> <ID2>:<ADDR2>
```
example: 

```BASH
branectl generate infra -f -p ./config/infra.yml client-node-1:145.100.135.172 client-node-2:145.100.135.241
```

### B.4 Generate Proxy Configuration:

```Bash
branectl generate proxy -f -p ./config/proxy.yml
```

### B.5 Generate Node Configuration: Generate the node.yml using your Control Node's hostname:

```Bash
branectl generate node -f central <HOSTNAME>
```

example

```Bash
branectl generate node -f central ab-01.uvalight.net
```

## Step C: Certificates

### C.1 The Control Node must be able to verify worker identities.

Navigate to ~/brane-central/config/certs/.

For each worker domain, create a subdirectory named after that domain.

Place the worker's public certificate inside that folder and rename it ca.pem.

## Step D: Launch

### D.1 Start the services using the local Docker daemon:

```Bash
branectl start central

# 3. Verification
Verify the system is operational by checking the active containers and logs:

List Containers: docker ps (Ensure all Brane containers are running).

Note: The brane-api service may crash until the Scylla database service is fully initialized; wait a minute or use watch docker ps.

Check Logs: If a service fails to start, inspect the logs using:

Bash
docker logs <container_name>
